SLUG RULES AND LIFECYCLE — MANDATORY
The slug column is a required field for every new story. Generate the slug from the final headline and explicitly include it in every INSERT. The live column is text, NOT NULL, UNIQUE, and limited to 60 characters. Its current database default is an empty string, and no active slug trigger was found during the latest metadata check. Therefore, do not rely on a database trigger or default to generate the correct slug. Supplying the generated slug yourself also remains compatible with a future trigger that fills the slug only when it is NULL.

Generate a slug using these rules, in this exact order:
1. Convert the headline to lowercase.
2. Strip accents and diacritics, so é becomes e and ñ becomes n.
3. Replace every ampersand (&) with the word "and".
4. Delete apostrophes without inserting a hyphen. For example, "Stranger's" becomes "strangers". Delete straight and typographic apostrophes.
5. Replace every consecutive run of characters outside a-z and 0-9 with exactly one hyphen. This includes spaces, colons, commas, quotation marks, dashes, slashes, and other punctuation.
6. Trim hyphens from the beginning and end.
7. Limit the slug to 60 characters. If it is longer than 60, cut at the last hyphen at or before character 60, excluding that hyphen so no word is split. If there is no hyphen in the first 60 characters, hard-cut at 60.
8. After truncation, trim any hyphens from both ends again. The final character MUST never be a hyphen. The first character MUST never be a hyphen either.
9. Keep all words, including small words such as "the" and "a". Keep all numbers. Do not remove stop words.

Examples:
- "Six Days Alone: The Teenager Who Refused to Give Up" -> "six-days-alone-the-teenager-who-refused-to-give-up"
- "A Stranger's Gift Gave Her a Second Chance" -> "a-strangers-gift-gave-her-a-second-chance"
- "The Neighbours Who Rebuilt a Community After the Flood" -> "the-neighbours-who-rebuilt-a-community-after-the-flood"
- "After 40 Years, Rescue Crews & Farmers Rebuild the Outback Airstrip They Lost to the Flood" -> "after-40-years-rescue-crews-and-farmers-rebuild-the-outback"

Uniqueness:
- Before inserting, check whether the generated slug already exists in undowned.stories.
- If it is free, use it as generated.
- If it already exists, append "-2", then "-3", then "-4", continuing with the first available integer suffix.
- Keep the complete slug, including a collision suffix, at no more than 60 characters. When space is needed for a suffix, shorten the base at a word boundary using the same last-hyphen rule, then append the suffix. Never leave a trailing hyphen before or after adding the suffix.
- Check the final candidate against existing slugs before insertion. The unique constraint remains the final safeguard. Never overwrite or update an existing row to resolve a slug collision.

Empty slug:
- If the headline produces an empty slug after normalization and cleanup (for example, a headline containing only non-Latin characters), do not insert a blank slug and do not invent a transliteration.
- If a user-provided or otherwise explicitly approved manual slug is available, validate it against the same 60-character, lowercase, a-z/0-9/hyphen, no-leading-or-trailing-hyphen, and uniqueness requirements, then use it.
- If no approved manual slug is available, skip that story and report that a manual slug is required.

